course: dictionary
lesson: 9793
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer chose. Suspend is one of these words. «The lamp was suspended from the ceiling by a chain.» The lamp is hanging from above, so suspended means hung up.
explain: «Matches were suspended because of the snow.» Nothing is hanging here. The matches were stopped for a while. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Matches were stopped for a while because of the snow" still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: A pupil can also be suspended. «When Jake was suspended for fighting, the school phoned his dad at the warehouse.» Here suspended means sent away from school for a set time as a punishment. The phone call and the fighting are your clues.
fact: To suspend something means to hang it up high, or to stop it for a time.
fact: «Suspended» can mean hung up, stopped for a while, or kept away from school or work for a time as a punishment.
fact: In science, tiny bits can be suspended in a liquid: they float through it and do not dissolve.
fact: «Suspend disbelief» means pretending, for a while, that a magic story is real.
fact: In the UK, a pupil who is suspended is often said to be «excluded» for a fixed time.
exercise: «The lamp was suspended from the ceiling by a chain.» What does suspended mean here? | Stopped for a while | *Hung up from above | Painted white | Sent home from school
exercise: «Matches were suspended because of the snow.» What does suspended mean here? | Cooked slowly | Painted red | *Stopped for a while | Hung from a hook
exercise: «When Jake was suspended for fighting, the school phoned his dad.» Find and copy the word that tells you what Jake was punished with. | *fighting | phoned | warehouse | suspended
test: What does «suspend disbelief» mean? | *Pretend for a while that a magic story is real | Believe every fact in a book | Stop reading the book | Fall asleep while reading
test: Tiny bits suspended in a liquid do what? | They dissolve straight away | They are poured out of the glass | *They float in it without dissolving | They turn the liquid into a solid
exam: Which sentence uses suspended to mean hung up from above? | The trains were suspended because of the storm. | Her homework was suspended until Friday. | *The lantern was suspended from a hook above the door. | The pupil was suspended for two days.
